{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789218131,"nonce":"RY6hBZz3PG+ZsgCZJpQ/5FDFEUY=","title":"A parameter reassigned in a loop read its original value every iteration","message":"SSA construction seeded every block's definitions with a copy of each\nparameter's entry value, under the comment \"parameters don't need phis\n(they're never reassigned)\". When one is reassigned, IDF placement puts\na phi in the loop header, but the body has no phi for it and reads the\nseeded copy instead of walking to the header. The write then computes\nfrom the original parameter, LICM hoists it to the entry as invariant,\nand the loop never terminates.\n\nReproducer: `def f(n: int): while n \u003e 0: n -= 3`. HIR shows `sub %n, 3`\nin the entry block and the header phi's back-edge value equal to it.\n\nFix: seed only parameters that scan_cfg_for_variable_writes reports as\nnever written; a written one is reached through its phi like any other\nvariable.","files":null}]}